# Audit log.
#
# Every line carries the SHA-256 of everything before it, and audit.log.head
# records how many entries there should be and what the last hash is. Editing,
# deleting or commenting out an entry is caught by one or the other.
#
# It is NOT tamper-proof. The digest takes only public inputs, so anyone with
# write access to both files can recompute the whole history. The anchor against
# that is version control: once these files are committed, a rewrite is a diff.
#
# Format: seq | timestamp | event | experiment | detail | chain hash
#
# Reading TEST requires an "unseal" entry recorded before the number is read.
0001 | 2026-08-26T03:05:45Z | create | registry | folds 60/20/20, preregistration and registry written | 029d4643f1303ffd19cec78c73b1472ca1eebd2f897bd6e8272c6cade6177445
